# =====================================================================
# .gitignore â€” versions CODE + partition indices (B7) + cohort tables + docs.
# Excludes raw data, large regenerable arrays, model weights, and mid-grid
# volatile outputs. See data/README.md to obtain the raw datasets.
# =====================================================================

# --- raw data (never committed; huge, external) ---
LIDC-IDRI/
LNDb/
LNDB/
data/
*.rar
*.mhd
*.raw
*.dcm

# --- large / regenerable arrays and weights (CRITICAL: exclude the .npy tree,
#     ~5.7 GB, and all model checkpoints) ---
outputs/processed/
*.npy
outputs/models/
outputs/**/*.pt
outputs/**/*.pth
outputs/metadata/*.pkl
outputs/metadata/processed_index_*.csv

# --- backups / archives / logs (not part of the released repo) ---
outputs/_archive_250/
outputs/_pre_remediation/
outputs/logs/

# --- POST-GRID (2026-07-27): the 740-patient grid is COMPLETE (150 runs, consistency gate exit 0),
#     so the artifacts below are no longer volatile and ARE committed, as planned. They are what
#     makes the reviewers' verifiability demand real: every reported number is regenerated from
#     these by the released code, with no GPU. Total ~11 MB.
#   outputs/probs/     per-sample y_true + y_prob, one .npz per run
#   outputs/history/   per-epoch train/val trajectory + the config stamp, one .json per run
#   outputs/metrics/   analysis outputs
#   outputs/results/   per-model tables, confusion matrices
#   outputs/figures/   generated figures
#
# Model WEIGHTS stay out (outputs/models/, 6.3 GB) and so do the preprocessed arrays
# (outputs/processed/, 8.2 GB): both are regenerable from the committed code + indices.

# --- committed ON PURPOSE (do NOT ignore): the executable partition indices
#     R3 asked for (B7), the cohort/accounting tables, code, config, docs ---
#   outputs/splits/            (partition indices â€” B7)
#   outputs/metadata/lidc_master.csv, lidc_nodules.csv, dataset_accounting.*

# --- generated report artifacts (regenerable from source) ---
*.pdf
Relatorio_*.html
# EXCEPTION: the manuscript figures travel with the paper (deterministic outputs of
# paper/figures/*.py; \includegraphics needs them present to compile).
!paper/2_resubmission/figures/*.pdf
!paper/2_resubmission/figures/*.png
# EXCEPTION: the PDF that was actually submitted and reviewed. This is provenance, not a build
# artifact -- it is the only record of exactly what the four reviewers read, and it cannot be
# regenerated (the manuscript it came from has since been rebuilt).
!paper/1_original_submission/submitted_manuscript.pdf

# --- python / os / editors ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
*.egg-info/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- stray scratch logs ---
*.log
# build output: the bibliography is inlined in the .tex, so a tracked .bbl would be a second
# copy of it, free to drift. See paper/2_resubmission/MAINTAINING.md.
*.bbl
*.err

# =====================================================================================
# NOT PUBLISHED (D69). These stay on disk and stay out of the repository.
# =====================================================================================
# Peer review is confidential by convention, so the reviewers' verbatim reports and the response
# document that quotes them are not published. Their version record lives outside git, as the
# date-stamped copies sync_shared.ps1 leaves in the coauthors' shared folder.
paper/reviewer_comments.md
# The decision letter as received. Confidential peer-review correspondence: it was
# untracked but NOT ignored until 2026-08-05, i.e. one `git add -A` from publication.
paper/reviewer_comments_verbatim.md
paper/**/response_to_reviewers.md
paper/**/Response-to-Reviewers.docx
paper/**/Resubmission-Checklist.docx
paper/**/IEEE-Access-Response-to-Reviewers-template.docx

# IEEE template scaffolding. The class and bibliography styles carry their own licence, and the
# Formata typeface shipped with the IEEE Access template is a commercial font licensed to IEEE, so
# neither is redistributed here. paper/README.md tells the reader to fetch the official template.
paper/**/IEEEtran.cls
paper/**/IEEEtran.bst
paper/**/ieeeaccess.cls
paper/**/spotcolor.sty
paper/**/t1-*
paper/**/logo.png
paper/**/bullet.png
paper/**/notaglinelogo.png

# Build and submission archives: containers whose contents are versioned individually.
paper/**/*.zip

# Superseded audit artifacts, which also recorded the author's user directory.
outputs/metrics/audit_raw.json
outputs/metrics/audit_findings.json

# --- INTERNAL WORKING MATERIAL, NOT PUBLISHED (researcher's instruction, 2026-07-28) ---
# docs/ is our workspace, not documentation: the decision log, the session journal, the running
# status, the methodology contract, run plans, and a draft letter to another dataset's authors. It is
# our context and history, and it stays local. Public documentation is README.md plus the READMEs in
# paper/, data/ and outputs/splits/.
CLAUDE.md
docs/
# Working backups and pre-strip copies. manuscript.tex.commented and references.bib.commented
# hold the 454 internal comments removed on 2026-08-09; committing them would republish exactly
# what the strip removed, the pending-CRediT block among it.
*.bak
*.bak_*
*.commented
*.generated_from_md.bak
# page renders kept for eyeballing a compile; not a deliverable
paper/**/_pdfcheck*/
